  "narrative": "These results assess the robustness of the central outcome_014 association with feature_027. The approximate 10% absolute clinical threshold for outcome_014 is about 0.0093 under the same operationalization used earlier. Every new feature_027 stratum contrast—H39/H67 by feature_034, H40/H68 by feature_002, H73/H74 by feature_050, H77 within feature_008=0, H58 within feature_054 level_002, and H80/H81 within feature_061 age extremes—has a point estimate around +0.78 to +0.80 and a lower 95% Welch bound far above both zero and the clinical threshold. The cells meet the minimum-count rule, although several are modest (for example feature_008=0, feature_061 extremes, and feature_050=1). Multiplicity is present, but the intervals are so far above the threshold that the pattern is highly unlikely to be explained by chance selection among these 12 tests. I therefore accept the feature_027 stratum associations and close their broad robustness work. This supports a stable dataset-specific association across measured covariate structures rather than an artifact confined to one subgroup, but it does not identify why the effect is so large or establish causality, biology, or generalizability. H86/H87 test whether feature_050 retains a negative association conditional on feature_027 status. Their signed estimates are small relative to the threshold in H86 and only weakly above it in H87, with intervals crossing zero and the threshold; I cannot accept or reject those clinically meaningful negative claims and defer them. No validation is requested because the original H14 effect has already been independently validated and these stratum estimates strongly replicate it internally.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 4 appraise: outcome_014 feature_027 association is robust across feature_034, feature_002, feature_050, feature_008=0, feature_054 level_002, and feature_061 age extremes. Accept H39, H67, H40, H68, H73, H74, H77, H58, H80, H81; close these stratum investigations. H86/H87 remain unresolved deferred because conditional feature_050 intervals are wide and include both null and threshold-crossing values. The huge H14 association remains an accepted dataset-specific association, not a causal/generalizable claim, and its opacity/latent structure remains unresolved. Next allocation: close broad feature_027 robustness work unless a new interaction/stratum contrast appears; run remaining untested feature_050 outcome screens or other predictors rather than continue H14-centered work unless validation or effect-modification tests become informative."
